// Golden lockstep replay: a real battle on the shipped default arena, with the world
// checksum recorded every `checkpoint_interval` ticks.
//
// Every target (Linux, Windows, macOS ARM64, wasm32-wasip1) replays this script and must
// reproduce `checksums` exactly. A simulation change that alters behaviour updates this
// list in the commit that explains why. See tests/golden_replay_tests.rs.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP4 (Q0036): "red_psi" (psi_grey) now
// swings with damage point 0, every 21 ticks, range 0.1, backswing 9 (was 4, 22, 0.3, 6).
// Checkpoints 1 to 4 (ticks 1 to 200) are unchanged; from checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to 250), the
// first in which the zealot weapon matters, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP6 (Q0038; marine damage point 1, backswing 13) from checkpoint 4 on, and
// for WP7 (Q0039): "blue_infantry" (pulse_bot) now walks at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09), so every
// checkpoint changed from checkpoint 1 (ticks 1 to 50), where the squad starts moving at tick 5.
// Re-recorded for WP8 (Q0039): the Overclock of "blue_infantry" (stimmed at tick 260) lasts 268
// ticks (was 250). Its remaining ticks are world state, so checkpoints 6 and 7 (ticks 251 to 350)
// changed; from checkpoint 8 on the checksums are those of WP7 again: no unit carries the
// Overclock by tick 400 (the stimmed marines have died), so the longer stim changed nothing else.
// Re-recorded for WP15 (Q0045 3b): "overclock_stim" now also unlocks the Overclock of
// shock_golem. The research is completed before tick 1 and each player's unlocked abilities are
// hashed, so every checkpoint changed; no unit's behaviour did (with the units.ron part of the
// change alone, every checkpoint stays as recorded for WP8).
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-battle-flipbook-animation WP2 (checksum schema 9 -> 10): each
// entity's `anim_progress`, a constant zero no system wrote, is no longer encoded, so every
// checkpoint changed. No behaviour did: the render snapshots of all 1000 ticks are byte for byte
// those of schema 9.
// Re-recorded for plan 2026-11-04-combat-sc2-alignment WP9 (D-4): the shield-regeneration delay
// is read from the catalog (still 250), and a new entity's `ticks_since_last_damage` starts at
// u16::MAX ("never damaged") instead of 250. That counter is hashed, so every checkpoint
// changed. No behaviour did: with the spawn value left at 250, every checkpoint stays as
// recorded for flipbook WP2.
// Re-recorded for WP10 (Q0039): every shielded archetype regenerates 0.112 shields per tick (was
// 0.08). Checkpoints 1 to 12 are unchanged; from checkpoint 13 (ticks 601 to 650), when a
// damaged "red_psi" zealot has first gone 250 ticks unhit, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP11 (Q0039): shields start regenerating 179 ticks after the last damage (was
// 250). Checkpoints 1 to 11 are unchanged; from checkpoint 12 (ticks 551 to 600), when that
// zealot now starts regenerating, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group S1 (Q0039): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) and "red_siege"
// (railgun_crawler) walk at 0.126 per tick (was 0.09, the Normal-time speed). Every checkpoint
// changed from checkpoint 1 (ticks 1 to 50), where "blue_armor" starts moving at tick 5.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group R2 (Q0039): "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) regenerates 0.01531 life
// per tick (was 0, the Roach's 0.2734 per Normal s). Only checkpoints 6 and 8 to 11 (ticks 251
// to 300 and 351 to 550) changed; checkpoints 1 to 5, 7 and 12 to 20 are as before (no
// regenerating beetle's life differs at those checkpoints).
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W1 (Q0039): "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) fires every 19 ticks in
// tank mode (was 26, the Normal-time period). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4
// (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight after the AttackMove of tick 120, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W2: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) fires every 36 ticks (was 28;
// StarCraft II's 2 Normal s). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to
// 200), the first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W3: "red_siege" (railgun_crawler) releases its shot 3 ticks into
// the swing (was 4, the Normal-time 0.167 s), in tank and siege mode. Checkpoints 1 to 3 are
// unchanged; from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W4: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) releases 3 ticks into its swing (was
// 2; the CWeapon default 0.167 Normal s). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from checkpoint 4
// (ticks 151 to 200), its first fight, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W5: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) and "red_siege" (railgun_crawler)
// have the CWeapon default backswing of 9 ticks (was 4). Checkpoints 1 to 3 are unchanged; from
// checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), their first fights, every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP12 group W7: "blue_armor" (rhino_beetle) throws its acid at 1.05 per tick (was
// 0.64; the Roach's missile, 18.75 Normal per s). Checkpoints 1 to 4 are unchanged; from
// checkpoint 5 (ticks 201 to 250), every checkpoint changed.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit b (D-8 item 4, Q0045 1b): the movement phase no longer snaps a
// turret to its goal; the weapon phase alone turns it, at its rate (21.6 degrees per tick for
// "red_siege", railgun_crawler). Turret angles are hashed, so checkpoints 4 to 6 and 9 (ticks 151
// to 300 and 401 to 450) changed. No behaviour did: with turret angles left out of the checksum,
// every checkpoint of both fixtures equals that of commit a.
// Re-recorded for WP17 commit d (audit §10.3): hull-mounted weapons fire within their StarCraft
// II tolerance (Arc / 2 + ArcSlop: 11.25 degrees for "blue_infantry", "blue_armor" and "red_psi",
// which fired within 15, 15 and 180). A unit whose target is outside it now turns first. Every
// checkpoint from checkpoint 4 (ticks 151 to 200), the first fight, changed.
(
    checksum_schema: 10,
    seed: 0x5EED_0F_5CAFF1E,
    total_ticks: 1000,
    checkpoint_interval: 50,
    squads: [
        (name: "blue_infantry", player: 0, slug: "pulse_bot", count: 16, origin: (18, 10), columns: 8),
